# Generated by the vNext CI workflow (reduced supported build graph).
.vnext-packages.txt

# Gate artifacts: each recorder directory holds an ephemeral signing key and a
# digest key (§21, §23). They stay out of git by design; the docs reproduce them.
/output/

# Local scratch: experiment by-products, handoff notes, downloaded fixtures.
# Untracked on purpose; it was committed once by a blanket `git add -A` and
# removed again in the next commit.
/tmp/

# Local scratch that a blanket `git add -A` once committed into history (54 tmp/ files, 5 examples/).
# /tmp/ and /output/ were already ignored; examples/ was the gap. The history carrying those
# blobs was scrubbed before the first push - see docs/system-design/vnext-history-scrub.md.
/examples/

# Committed build outputs. `go build -o <pkg>/<name>` drops the binary next to its
# sources, and nothing ignored that path: cmd/evidra-gatea/evidra-gatea (9.7 MB) was
# committed with the Gate A runner, and evidra-exp (9.5 MB) came in with a 0.5.1 version bump.
# Neither is referenced by any build, test or doc. The Makefile writes to bin/ instead.
/cmd/evidra-gatea/evidra-gatea
/evidra-exp
